WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.480
If you want to see pretty much 100% proof
that Sister Irene from The Nun is related

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:10.360
to Lorraine Warren from the Conjuring,
then stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.440
[intro]

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.780
Welcome back to Things You Missed.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.010
If you haven’t already seen the initial
episode, 34 Things You Missed in The Nun -- you’ll

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.460
want to watch that before watching this video.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.189
I mean, I guess there’s no reason you have
to watch them in order -- but the reason I

00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:29.849
say that is I don’t want a million people
to comment on this video telling me the things

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:33.070
that I missed that I already covered in the
other video.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:36.590
One of the first shots we see in the Abbey
is a cross with an infinity symbol in the

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:37.590
middle.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:41.330
Later on, we see imagery of the snakes, the
symbol of Valak, forming the same symbol as

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:42.330
well.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:45.920
This may or may not be related to something
known as the Leviathan cross, which looks

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.170
like this and is sometimes used as a Satanic
symbol.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.640
During the opening scene, when the Nuns are
attacked by Valak, Sister Jessica mentions

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.700
an important detail that plays into the twist
ending.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:56.750
“Take it!

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:00.430
This evil needs a vessel to escape!”

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:05.430
That’s the reason that Sister Victoria sacrifices
herself, and the reason that Valak is able

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:08.790
to escape the abbey at the end, using Frenchie
as a vessel.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.780
You gotta feel bad for Frenchie.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:15.040
He’s just minding his own business, finds
a body, probably gets demonetized for it,

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:21.510
then LITERALLY gets demonetized, aka possessed
by a demon… alright clearly this pun isn’t

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.850
going anywhere, so I’m gonna move on to
the next Thing You Missed.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:27.580
So in the other video I pointed out a few
of the hidden Valak messages at the beginning

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:30.130
of the film, and now I’ve found a couple
more.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:33.810
In the classroom where we first meet Sister
Irene, there are some letters on the wall.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:37.800
The shape of the chairs right here creates
the V, then if you go up from there you’ll

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:38.800
find the A-L-A-K.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.510
Valak.

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:43.360
Valak is also written wayyy in the background
on the board.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:47.710
Now that The Nun is out on Blu-Ray I have
the power to pause and take a closer look

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:50.100
at all the words written in Father Burke’s
crossword puzzle.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.090
Here are the ones I found to be significant.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:57.490
Annointer -- that’s someone who applies
ritualistic oil during a religious ceremony.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:58.490
In The Nun…

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:02.620
I mean it’s not oil, but Sister Irene is
protected by the blood of the holy grail being

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:06.299
smeared on her forehead, so I feel like there’s
something there.

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:09.709
Aimless -- that’s a word you could use to
describe Frenchie at the beginning of the

00:02:09.709 --> 00:02:11.480
story.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.799
"What is it?"

00:02:16.799 --> 00:02:20.340
"Mr Devoe?"

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.120
"Hi..."

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:26.300
And novice -- this one describes Sister Irene
because she’s young and hasn’t taken her

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.409
vows.

00:02:27.409 --> 00:02:31.019
Sister Irene helps him fill in the next word,
“deliveries”, and if you think about it,

00:02:31.019 --> 00:02:35.100
this may be more than just an instance of
her holy crossword solving skills, but also

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.379
a psychic vision, because they end up going
to the deliveries room at the Abbey.

00:02:39.379 --> 00:02:40.379
“The icehouse.

00:02:40.379 --> 00:02:44.510
It’s where I leave my deliveries.”

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.829
Father Burke and Sister Irene are asked to
stay overnight to talk to the other Nuns in

00:02:47.829 --> 00:02:48.829
the morning.

00:02:48.829 --> 00:02:52.519
During the night, the father is lured out
into the cemetery by the form of a young boy

00:02:52.519 --> 00:02:56.129
he performed an exorcism on years before named
Daniel.

00:02:56.129 --> 00:03:00.019
If you pause right on the moment the father
shines his flashlight on Daniel, you’ll

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:04.439
notice his eyes are glowing white, similar
to how sister Irene looks later on when she’s

00:03:04.439 --> 00:03:05.439
having a vision.

00:03:05.439 --> 00:03:09.760
The father ends up being buried alive by Valak,
but thanks to Sister Irene’s abilities as

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:13.309
a medium, she’s able to rescue him, and
they find these books in the coffin.

00:03:13.309 --> 00:03:17.499
Two of the books have snake eyes on them,
which is notable because Valak is sometimes

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.940
referred to as the marquis of snakes.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.060
"Valak.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:24.860
The defiler.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:26.480
The profane.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:30.180
The marquis of snakes."

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:34.920
...and you’ll later see plenty of snake
imagery when Father Burke sits down to study

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.040
the books.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:39.510
Wait, hold on… roll back on that for a sec.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.749
I think we can use that clip in our next chillhop
video.

00:03:41.749 --> 00:03:48.510
I can just imagine the title: “Lo-Fi Chillhop
for Studying / Chilling / Performing an Exorcism.”

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:52.290
I’ve talked previously about how Valak is
a character in the real-world book The Lesser

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:57.169
Key of Solomon, but in that book he looks
more like this, and not really like a Nun.

00:03:57.169 --> 00:04:01.559
The books do have some shadowy images of a
more traditional looking demons so I wonder

00:04:01.559 --> 00:04:04.370
if those pictures represent the true form
of Valak.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:08.000
Or maybe Valak is just a big Brendon Urie
fan, I don’t know.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:11.870
The other document that the father studies
is the map of the abbey, which is labeled

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:15.370
“Castelui Sarpe”, Romanian for “Castle
Snake”.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:20.280
The map also reveals the locations where Valak
stalks the halls at night, like this tunnel,

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.599
where Sister Irene is later attacked.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.500
“Oh God.”

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.370
Where does all this wind come from anyway?

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.620
Does Valak just have the ability to create
wind?

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.110
I mean we see the same thing in The Conjuring
2, but it makes more sense cause there is

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:35.370
a storm outside.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:40.169
Anyway, when Sister Irene finds Sister Oana’s
body in the chapel, you can see that her hands

00:04:40.169 --> 00:04:44.979
have been impaled, painting the grim picture
that she’s been crucified.

00:04:44.979 --> 00:04:48.830
During Valak’s attack on the abbey, Father
Burke is investigating off on his own, and

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.610
I noticed what I think is a mistake.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:53.889
It looks like they tried to steal a shot from
another scene or something.

00:04:53.889 --> 00:04:59.920
The Father is supposed to be by himself at
this point in the movie… but who’s this?

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:03.210
Also during the attack while Sister Irene
is praying with the other Nuns, there is a

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:07.759
quick cutaway shot to this statue, and the
baby has wings, making it look a lot more

00:05:07.759 --> 00:05:10.810
like Valak’s appearance in the Lesser Key
of Solomon.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.889
After the incident is over, the wings are
no longer visible.

00:05:13.889 --> 00:05:17.220
Shortly after that we get one more look at
Father Burke’s crossword puzzle.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:22.409
There are a couple pairs of opposites: execute
&amp; create, obvious references to Christ, and

00:05:22.409 --> 00:05:26.590
dawn &amp; dusk, possibly related to the fact
that the nuns take a vow of silence from dusk

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.590
until dawn.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:30.289
He’s also penned in the word reflective.

00:05:30.289 --> 00:05:33.720
You may remember that when Frenchy goes to
the pub in town, they mention that they cover

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.699
all the mirrors after a death so that the
ghost won’t see it’s reflection.

00:05:37.699 --> 00:05:41.389
Sister Irene’s first encounter with Valak
is through a mirror in the chapel.

00:05:41.389 --> 00:05:44.750
The last word I noticed on the crossword puzzle
is “Wan”.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:49.440
The film that started it all, The Conjuring,
and it’s sequel, The Conjuring 2 are directed

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:50.860
by James Wan.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:54.760
Alright… this last one is maybe the biggest
Thing You Missed I’ve ever done.

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:59.430
If I gave out a golden magnifying glass to
the best Thing You Missed, it would go to

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:01.070
this Thing You Missed.

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:05.180
There’s been a theory floating around about
the possible relation between Sister Irene

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:08.410
from The Nun and Lorraine Warren from The
Conjuring.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:12.590
Both are mediums, and both have intense visions
of past, present and future.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:15.500
Both have visions and some kind of tie to
Valak.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:19.370
It seems reasonable to suggest that this is
a trait that can run in the family, due to

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:22.950
the fact that Lorraine’s daughter Judy also
has visions of the Nun.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:26.569
The Vatican tells Father Burke to take Sister
Irene with him on his journey, because she

00:06:26.569 --> 00:06:28.259
supposedly knows the area.

00:06:28.259 --> 00:06:33.180
However, upon meeting her, he finds she does
not know the area, but Father Burke claims

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:36.240
the church must have a reason for selecting
her.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:39.600
"Every decision the Vatican makes is with
purpose.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:44.100
I'm sure they had their reasons for selecting you."

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:48.120
Finally there’s the fact that the real life
actresses that play Sister Irene and Lorraine

00:06:48.129 --> 00:06:50.379
Warren are sisters in real life.

00:06:50.379 --> 00:06:54.100
Some have speculated that they’re sisters
in the movie, some say they are the same person

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:58.050
and Sister Irene changes her name later in
life, while some think their similarities

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.849
are just coincidence.

00:06:59.849 --> 00:07:05.879
However, in The Nun, I think Sister Irene’s
passport would prove otherwise.

00:07:05.879 --> 00:07:12.009
Irene Palmer was born on March 2nd 1930 about
three years after Lorraine's date of birth.

00:07:12.009 --> 00:07:16.340
Lorraine Warren’s maiden name is Moran,
so that might throw out the theory that they’re

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:20.870
sisters, however, Irene’s place of birth
is listed as Bridgeport, Connecticut -- which

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:24.699
happens to be exactly where Lorraine Warren
was born.

00:07:24.699 --> 00:07:30.340
There may be further connections in the deleted
scenes of The Nun, so make sure you subscribe

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:34.909
to CZsWorld to stay up to date on all the
Things You Missed, ring the deathbell for

00:07:34.909 --> 00:07:38.660
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:41.739
Assuming, we both survive.

